i.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101991","id":2613440346,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6bxe9a","user":{"login":"btgs-0","id":149745752,"node_id":"U_kgDOCOzwWA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/149745752?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/btgs-0","html_url":"https://github.com/btgs-0","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btgs-0/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btgs-0/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btgs-0/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btgs-0/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btgs-0/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btgs-0/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btgs-0/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btgs-0/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/btgs-0/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-24T21:51:07Z","updated_at":"2025-01-24T21:51:07Z","body":"Correct me if I'm misunderstanding, but I think I see why this functions the way it does. A user may not necessarily want an underlying script change to cascade to all child resources. What if you had: \n\n- enemy_health.tres: value = 100\n- enemy_2_health.tres: value = 30\n- player_health.tres: value = 45\n \nChanging the underlying health_resource.gd script would wipe out all of the values set for each resource, wouldn't it? i.e. \nchanging health_resource.gd value = 10 would mean: \n\n- enemy_health.tres: value = 10\n- enemy_2_health.tres: value = 10\n- player_health.tres: value = 10","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2613440346/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3577673562","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101991#issuecomment-3577673562","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101991","id":3577673562,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VPvda","user":{"login":"klianc09","id":11250609,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjUwNjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11250609?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09","html_url":"https://github.com/klianc09","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-25T21:32:56Z","updated_at":"2025-11-25T21:32:56Z","body":"I can confirm this still happens in v4.5.1.stable.official [f62fdbde1] but only with the setup in the bug.zip above (where no separate .gd file is created but only an \"inline\" script that's stored in the resource (idk what's the official name for that).\nWhen the script is stored in a separate .gd script then this issue does not appear.\n\n\n> Correct me if I'm misunderstanding, but I think I see why this functions the way it does. A user may not necessarily want an underlying script change to cascade to all child resources. \n\nThis is regarding default values, when no explicit value has been set in the child resources. You want default values to cascade, or else what's the point of default values. ","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3577673562/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3583147142","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101991#issuecomment-3583147142","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101991","id":3583147142,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VknyG","user":{"login":"Nallebeorn","id":7013489,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMTM0ODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7013489?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn","html_url":"https://github.com/Nallebeorn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-26T20:40:50Z","updated_at":"2025-11-26T20:40:50Z","body":"From what I can tell this only happens because running the project (or pressing Ctrl+S) doesn't save the resource's built-in script (which you can tell from the (*) in the script list if you expand it enough). The inspector updates even without saving the script, but `new_resource.tres` doesn't. If you explicitly save the built-in script (Ctrl+Alt+S, or File->Save) before running, the new value is printed correctly.\n\nThis would make this issue a consequence of #113166 that @klianc09 just raised.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3583147142/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3583558077","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101991#issuecomment-3583558077","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101991","id":3583558077,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VmMG9","user":{"login":"klianc09","id":11250609,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjExMjUwNjA5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/11250609?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09","html_url":"https://github.com/klianc09","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/klianc09/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-26T23:42:13Z","updated_at":"2025-11-26T23:42:13Z","body":"Yeah that makes sense.\n\nThe initial issue (CASE A: for the case when the script is in a .gd file, just as described in the OP) was still present in v4.4.1 (which was the version I initially encountered the issue with) but has since been fixed in v4.5.1.\n\nNow, CASE B (the case with the built-in script) is definitely related to #113166 but not completely the same. The remaining problem here isn't that the resource doesn't save, but that the inspector shows the new value already, although the script didn't actually save yet. (but maybe fixing that should also be part of #113166, IDK)","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3583558077/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3587052947","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/101991#issuecomment-3587052947","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101991","id":3587052947,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc7VzhWT","user":{"login":"Nallebeorn","id":7013489,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjcwMTM0ODk=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/7013489?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn","html_url":"https://github.com/Nallebeorn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Nallebeorn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T19:02:20Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T19:02:20Z","body":"> The remaining problem here isn't that the resource doesn't save, but that the inspector shows the new value already, although the script didn't actually save yet.\n\nI'm not sure the inspector showing the new value without saving is a bug. On its own, that seems quite intuitive and convenient, and it behaves the same when editing exports in a standalone script. Not really familiar with the internals, but I think the inspector simply updates as soon as the script is reparsed -- the delay is affected by `idle_parse_delay` for example, so it happens at the same time as error checking.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3587052947/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]